We adopt a multivariate Gaussian likelihood function of the form
\begin{equation}
    \label{eq2:likelihood}
    \log(L(\alpha, \beta)) \sim (V_{ij} - V_{ij}^{\rm simu}) (V_{ij} - V_{ij}^{\rm simu})^* / \sigma^2
\end{equation}
Here, we assume that $\alpha$ and $\beta$ satisfy a uniform distribution, and $\sigma$ is the standard deviation of the thermal noise, which is determined by observing an `empty' sky region devoid of bright radio source.
